    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds **ADR-046: Logging Infrastructure**. **Documentation only.** Implementation (3 commits, ~500 lines) lands in a follow-up PR.\n\n**Zero existing debug prints** in the project — every diagnostic session during ADR-040 → ADR-045 was add-prints → rebuild → reproduce → read → remove-prints → rebuild. This ADR adds permanent, gated logging to end that cycle.\n\n## Measurement (source tree, 2026-10-29)\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `fprintf(stderr)` / `std::cerr` / `std::clog` in `src/` | **0** |\n| `getenv` usage | **0** |\n| `#ifdef DEBUG` / `CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE` conditionals | **0** |\n| Main entry | `src/main.cpp:6` |\n| `honeybee_lib` CMake target | Includes `base/version.cpp`, `base/url.cpp` — pattern for `base/log.cpp` |\n\n**Clean slate.** Purely additive. One CMake line.\n\n## API shape\n\n### Categories (7) × Levels (5)\n\n```cpp\nenum class LogCategory { Pipeline, Css, Cascade, Layout, Paint, Fetch, Event };\nenum class LogLevel { Error, Warn, Info, Debug, Trace };\n```\n\n### Functions\n\n```cpp\nvoid log_init() noexcept;           // called from main() once\nvoid log_set_config(...) noexcept;  // programmatic (tests)\nbool log_enabled(cat, lvl) noexcept; // hot path, 3 atomics\nvoid log_writev(cat, lvl, file, line, fmt, ...) noexcept;\n```\n\n### Macro\n\n```cpp\nHB_LOG(Layout, Debug, \"child_count=%d\", n);\n```\n\nZero cost when disabled: single branch, no formatting, no allocation.\n\n## Env vars\n\n| Variable | Example | Default |\n|---|---|---|\n| `HONEYBEE_LOG` | `layout,paint,fetch` or `all` | (unset = disabled) |\n| `HONEYBEE_LOG_LEVEL` | `error|warn|info|debug|trace` | `debug` when set |\n| `HONEYBEE_LOG_FILE` | `/tmp/hb.log` | stderr |\n\n**Three vars, not one composite** — matches `RUST_LOG` / `MOZ_LOG` conventions.\n\n**Output format**:\n```\n[honeybee][layout][debug] src/renderer/layout/layout.cpp:482 child_count=3\n```\n\nGreppable by category: `grep '\\[layout\\]'`.\n\n## Scope (3 commits)\n\n### Commit 1 — Infrastructure\n- `src/base/log.{hpp,cpp}`\n- `LogCategory`, `LogLevel`, `log_init`, `log_set_config`, `log_enabled`, `log_writev`, `HB_LOG` macro\n- Env var parsing + file path trimming + thread-safe write\n- `log_init()` call in `main.cpp` at entry\n- `tests/test_log.cpp` (~12 tests)\n- **Behavior-neutral** — no log points yet\n\n### Commit 2 — Retrofit log points\n- ~15-20 `HB_LOG` sites across 7 files:\n  - `main.cpp` — startup\n  - `render_pipeline.cpp` — cache/cascade/layout/paint counts\n  - `async_fetcher.cpp` — fetch lifecycle\n  - `cascade.cpp` — rules matched\n  - `layout.cpp` — dispatch mode\n  - `paint.cpp` — box count\n  - `net/client.cpp` — HTTP request URLs, status codes\n- Manual verification across 6 env-var combinations\n\n### Commit 3 — Docs\n- ADR-046 → Implemented\n- README env-var section\n- CHANGELOG entry\n\n## Design decisions worth flagging\n\n- [ ] **Runtime-gated, not `#ifdef DEBUG`** — enables logging with `export HONEYBEE_LOG=...` without rebuild. Cost when disabled: ~1ns per call (single atomic read). Massive observability win.\n- [ ] **printf-style, not `std::format`** — matches project's existing C-style idioms (GTK, lexbor); `##__VA_ARGS__` works on GCC/Clang; no `<format>` dependency (libstdc++ 13.0+ only). If you prefer stream-style (`<<`), this is the one decision to push back on before Commit 1.\n- [ ] **7 categories** — enough granularity to isolate layout vs paint, cascade vs css; not so granular each new call site needs a decision.\n- [ ] **3 env vars** — `HONEYBEE_LOG` (categories), `_LEVEL` (severity), `_FILE` (redirect). Separate rather than composite (`layout:debug`) for typability.\n- [ ] **`log_set_config` for tests** — env vars leak between tests via `setenv`/`unsetenv`; programmatic API gives full isolation. `tmpfile()` for output capture.\n\n## Deferred (per ADR)\n\n- `std::format` migration (future ADR-047)\n- Runtime config reload\n- Log rotation (external `logrotate`)\n- Structured (JSON) output\n- Per-category thresholds\n- Trace-level perf timing\n\n## Test plan\n\nNo code touched. Post-merge: `cmake --build build && ./build/tests/honeybee_tests` — 572 / 2224 unchanged.\n\n## ADR\n\n`docs/decisions/046-logging.md` — status Accepted; implementation in follow-up PR.\n\nRefs #220\n",
